                <pb facs="0906" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./56</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 4.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1861</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    cablegram No. 26 [<hi rendition="#italic">21</hi>] of March 16, 5 p.m.
                    instructing the Legation to render all possible and <pb facs="0907" n="779"
                        xml:id="pg779"/> proper assistance to Mr. John D. MacGregor, Vice President
                    of the Pan American Airways Incorporated, in his effort to obtain a transport
                    concession, I have the honor to report, that I arranged for the President of
                    Guatemala to receive Mr. MacGregor today, and that since then he has informed
                    me, that he has had a very pleasant preliminary talk with President Chacón
                    concerning his project, and that he will visit the Minister of the Interior (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fomento</hi>) tomorrow, as suggested by the President,
                    for the purpose of discussing details.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur H.
                    Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
